# js-string-equals
  id: js-string-equals
  params: |first|, |second|
  head: When this builtin is invoked with parameters |first| and |second|, the following steps must be run:
  If(|first| is not null, and |first| is not a String)
    Throw(a {{RuntimeError}} exception as if a [=trap=] was executed)
  If(|second| is not null, and |second| is not a String)
    Throw(a {{RuntimeError}} exception as if a [=trap=] was executed)
  If([=!=] [=IsStrictlyEqual=](|first|, |second|) is true)
    Return(1)
  Return(0)

# js-string-compare
  id: js-string-compare
  params: |first|, |second|
  head: When this builtin is invoked with parameters |first| and |second|, the following steps must be run:
  Let(|first|, [=?=] [$UnwrapString$](|first|))
  Let(|second|, [=?=] [$UnwrapString$](|second|))
  If([=!=] [=IsStrictlyEqual=](|first|, |second|) is true)
    Return(0)
  If([=!=] [=IsLessThan=](|first|, |second|, true) is true)
    Return(-1)
  Return(1)

# a new promise
  params: |realm|
  head: To <dfn export lt="a new promise">create</dfn> a new <code><a interface>Promise</a>&lt;<var ignore>T</var>&gt;</code> in a [=realm=] |realm|, perform the following steps:
  Let(|constructor|, |realm|.[[Intrinsics]].[[%Promise%]])
  Return([=?=] [$NewPromiseCapability$](|constructor|))

# resolve
  params: |T|, |p|, |x|
  head: To <dfn export>resolve</dfn> a <code><a interface>Promise</a>&lt;|T|&gt;</code> |p| with |x| (a value of type |T|), perform the following steps:
  If(|x| is not ?(given))
    Let(?(it), ?(the {{undefined}} value))
  Let(|value|, [=converted to a JavaScript value=](|x|))
  Perform([=!=]([$Call$](|p|.[[Resolve]], ?(<emu-val>undefined</emu-val>), « |value| »)))
  If(|T| is ?({{undefined}}))
    ?(the |x| argument is optional, allowing a simpler "[=resolve=] p" usage)

# reject
  params: |p|, |r|
  head: To <dfn export>reject</dfn> a <code><a interface>Promise</a>&lt;<var ignore>T</var>&gt;</code> |p| with reason |r| (a JavaScript value), perform the following steps:
  Perform([=!=]([$Call$](|p|.[[Reject]], ?(<emu-val>undefined</emu-val>), « |r| »)))

# react
  params: |T|, |promise|
  head: To <dfn id="dfn-perform-steps-once-promise-is-settled" export lt="react|reacting" for="promise">react</dfn> to a <code><a interface>Promise</a>&lt;|T|&gt;</code> |promise|, given one or two sets of steps to perform, covering when the promise is fulfilled, rejected, or both, perform the following steps:
  Let(|onFulfilledSteps|, ?(the following steps given argument |V|:))
    Let(|value|, [=converted to an IDL value=](|V|, |T|))
    If(?(there) is ?(a set of steps to be run if the promise was fulfilled))
      Let(|result|, ?(performing them, given |value| if |T| is not {{undefined}}))
    Else
      Let(|result|, |value|)
    Return(?(|result|, [=converted to a JavaScript value=]))
  Let(|onFulfilled|, ?([$CreateBuiltinFunction$](|onFulfilledSteps|, 1, "", « »):))
  Let(|onRejectedSteps|, ?(the following steps given argument |R|:))
    Let(|reason|, [=converted to an IDL value=](|R|))
    If(?(there) is ?(a set of steps to be run if the promise was rejected))
      Let(|result|, ?(performing them, given |reason|))
    Else
      Let(|result|, [=a promise rejected with=](|reason|))
    Return(?(|result|, [=converted to a JavaScript value=]))
  Let(|onRejected|, ?([$CreateBuiltinFunction$](|onRejectedSteps|, 1, "", « »):))
  Let(|constructor|, |promise|.[[Promise]].[[Realm]].[[Intrinsics]].[[%Promise%]])
  Let(|newCapability|, [=?=] [$NewPromiseCapability$](|constructor|))
  Note(Not all callers will use the returned {{Promise}} Implementations might wish to avoid creating |newCapability| in those cases)
  Perform([$PerformPromiseThen$](|promise|.\[[Promise]], |onFulfilled|, |onRejected|, |newCapability|))
  Return(|newCapability|)
  Note(This algorithm will behave in a very similar way to the {{%Promise.prototype.then%|promise.then()}} method In particular, if the steps return a value of type |U| or <code><a interface>Promise</a>&lt;|U|&gt;</code>, this algorithm returns a <code><a interface>Promise</a>&lt;|U|&gt;</code> as well)

